{:tier :glm-5.2, :verse 44, :comments ["<b>ויעפילו.</b> In the language of (Isaiah 32:14) ״עופל ובחן״ — meaning that they went up onto the עופל (mound/fortress). And its midrashic sense is like ויאפילו, from the root אופל (darkness), meaning they went in darkness without permission and in a wicked way." "<b>וארון ברית ה' ומשה.</b> Scripture equated Moses to the Ark of the Covenant. And likewise it is written (Numbers 11:21) ״ויאמר משה שש מאות אלף רגלי״, and this is among the scriptural allusions, for Scripture joined Moses to ״six hundred thousand on foot״ to tell you that Moses was equivalent to sixty myriads, for if not, it would have been proper to say ״the people in the midst of whom I am — six hundred thousand on foot.״"], :book :numbers, :voice :rabbeinu-bahya, :lang :en, :chapter 14, :notes {}, :source-witnesses [{"versionTitle" "Sefaria community Hebrew (PD)", "language" "he"}], :timestamp "2026-07-30T14:32:37.763327993Z", :translated-from :he, :model "glm-5.2"}